mode: "100644"
text: "# Campaigns & launches 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (platform features + launch tactics move).*\n\n## The POV: the spotlight event, told as one story\nYour content calendar **keeps the lights on**; a **campaign is the spotlight event** — time-boxed, with\nplanned phases + dedicated assets toward **one primary goal.** The strongest launches run a **three-part\nfunnel — pre-launch → launch → post-launch (tease → launch → sustain)** — told as **ONE story**, not three\nseparate campaigns by different people. The classic failure: **pushing hard in week one, then going quiet\nwhile customers are still deciding.**\n\n## Pre-launch — build anticipation + collect intent\n- **Anticipation is the engine** (Apple orchestrates it; the Zeigarnik effect — people fixate on unfinished\n  narratives). The goal isn't awareness, it's **emotional investment**: when the audience wants it before it\n  exists, **launch day becomes a confirmation, not a cold intro.**\n- **Waitlist** = the cleanest mechanism (launches with real pre-launch marketing see **~30% higher day-one\n  sales** — Waitlister; vendor, directional, verify-quarterly). Make the promise specific\n  (\"first access to the beta + a launch-week discount\" > \"join the waitlist\"). A **referral waitlist** adds\n  momentum (unique links, reward referrals).\n- **One campaign hub:** every profile link (X pin, IG bio, LinkedIn featured, email signature) points to the\n  **same** hub (waitlist + offer + referral + proof). Don't make people hunt.\n- **BTS/teasers/proof drops** (\"people follow launches because they like watching things get built\").\n  **Beta/early-access group** (50–200 from the waitlist) for validation + proof. **Personalized press/creator\n  outreach** (10–20 relevant, with early access — **not** a mass press release).\n\n## Launch — concentrate conversion behind one CTA\n- **Velocity is rewarded:** app-store/social algorithms + press cycles reward **concentrated attention in a\n  short window** — a coordinated push across channels in a single morning beats the same activities spread\n  over a week. (Threads hit 100M in 5 days via coordinated activation — the principle scales down.)\n- **One CTA, remove friction** — landing page, ad copy, email, checkout/signup all point to **one action**;\n  don't split traffic across offers.\n- **Credible urgency only:** artificial/resetting countdowns **erode trust**. Use **real scarcity** (first\n  100), **meaningful bonuses** over deep discounts, an honest deadline; \"when urgency is real, conversions\n  spike — especially the final 24 hours.\" **Timed drops, countdowns, livestreams** create the peak moment.\n\n## Post-launch — reinforce with proof + sustain\n- **This is where teams compound trust or confirm it was noise.** Convert attention into **proof**:\n  testimonials, UGC, demos, objection-answers, FAQs. **Sustain** community engagement; mind the gap between\n  **\"signed up\" and \"used meaningfully\"** (simplify onboarding). Debrief: numbers vs targets, what\n  worked/broke, thank early adopters.\n\n## Launch types + orchestration + discipline\n- **Soft** (limited/controlled group — lower risk, real feedback) · **Hard** (full audience at once,\n  multi-channel + press — needs high confidence) · **Phased** (progressive by segment/geo/use-case — learn\n  + adjust).\n- **Focus on 1–3 platforms**; **repurpose, don't copy** (a 60s video → 15s Story / 9:16 TikTok / 30s\n  LinkedIn cut, each optimized); channels **reinforce** each other; **1–2 hero posts per phase** + evergreen\n  support. Run a **parallel email sequence** (teaser → priority-access → launch → objection → onboarding →\n  proof), segmented (VIP early access).\n- **Discipline over speed:** a **one-page launch brief** to all teams + a readiness meeting (timeline,\n  owners, blockers); **map the campaign week-by-week**; readiness checks (QA, support, checkout, analytics).\n  \"Without a clear timeline, campaigns drift.\" **Metrics:** day-one conversions, waitlist signups, referral\n  behavior, engagement, traffic, **ROI per channel**, numbers vs targets.\n"
